{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CeHh7132AmEcsobDUtF61","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gate is **partially broken**. Here's what I found:\n\n**What's wired correctly:**\n- `settings.json` has a `PreToolUse` hook on `Edit|Write` → `scripts/decisions-guard.sh` ✓\n- The script blocks `Edit` calls to `_ops/DECISIONS.md` with a `deny` ✓\n\n**The hole:**\n`decisions-guard.sh:13` only denies when `tool == \"Edit\"`. When the tool is `Write`, it falls through the `if` block and exits 0 — emitting no `permissionDecision`, which the harness treats as **allow**. A `Write` call can completely overwrite `DECISIONS.md` with arbitrary content, erasing history. The comment on line 11 says Write is safe because \"old content arrives as a prefix,\" but the script never verifies that — it just lets it through.\n\nThe gate claim in `GATES.md` (\"runs on every file edit, log shows it firing daily\") is overstated. It fires, but it only half-enforces the invariant.\n\n**Fix — add a `Write` block to the guard:**\n\n```bash\nif [ \"$tool\" = \"Edit\" ] || [ \"$tool\" = \"Write\" ]; then\n```\n\nOr more robustly, deny any tool that touches the file and isn't a known-safe append path (though Write has no safe append path — you'd need a dedicated append script).\n\n---\n\n**Also flagging from the startup hook:** There's no `UPGRADES.md` here, so there's no migration record. The skill is at 0.4.6 per `CLAUDE.md`; the hook says the current version is 0.4.8. If you want to migrate before cutting the release, I'd run `/upgrade` — but the gate hole above is the more immediate blocker.\n\nDo you want me to patch `decisions-guard.sh` now?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":729,"cache_read_input_tokens":30409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":729},"output_tokens":12,"service_tier":"standard","inf